    ingredients: [{"item": "Boneless center-cut pork chop", "unit": "oz", "quantity": "8"}, {"item": "Sugar-free uncured bacon", "unit": "slices", "quantity": "3"}, {"item": "White sweet potato, cubed", "unit": "medium", "quantity": "1"}, {"item": "Zucchini, sliced", "unit": "medium", "quantity": "1"}, {"item": "Extra virgin olive oil", "unit": "tbsp", "quantity": "1"}, {"item": "Sea salt", "unit": "tsp", "quantity": "1/2"}, {"item": "Dried sage", "unit": "tsp", "quantity": "1/2"}, {"item": "Garlic powder", "unit": "tsp", "quantity": "1/4"}, {"item": "Dried thyme", "unit": "tsp", "quantity": "1/4"}, {"item": "Fresh lemon juice", "unit": "tbsp", "quantity": "1"}],
    instructions: '1. SEASON THE PORK CHOP: Pat the pork chop dry. Season with sea salt, sage, garlic powder, and thyme.\n\n2. WRAP WITH BACON: Lay 3 slices of bacon on a cutting board, slightly overlapping. Place the pork chop at one end and roll to wrap. Secure with toothpicks if needed.\n\n3. PREP THE SIDES: Cube the white sweet potato into 1/2-inch pieces. Slice the zucchini into 1/4-inch rounds.\n\n4. ROAST THE SWEET POTATO: Toss sweet potato cubes with half the olive oil and a pinch of salt. Roast at 400F for 15 minutes.\n\n5. SEAR THE PORK: Heat remaining olive oil in an oven-safe skillet over medium-high heat. Sear the bacon-wrapped pork chop 2-3 minutes per side until bacon is crispy.\n\n6. ADD ZUCCHINI AND FINISH: Add the zucchini to the pan around the pork chop. Transfer skillet to 400F oven and bake 12-15 minutes until pork reaches 145F internal temperature.\n\n7. REST AND SERVE: Let pork rest 5 minutes. Serve with roasted sweet potato and zucchini. Drizzle with fresh lemon juice.',
