    name: 'Bison & Veggie Stir Fry with Avocado',
    ingredients: [{"item": "Ground bison", "unit": "lb", "quantity": "1"}, {"item": "Fresh broccoli", "unit": "cups", "notes": "cut into small florets", "quantity": "2-3"}, {"item": "Zucchini", "unit": "medium-large", "notes": "halved and sliced into half-moons", "quantity": "1"}, {"item": "Avocado", "unit": "whole", "notes": "sliced, for topping", "quantity": "1"}, {"item": "Avocado oil or coconut oil", "unit": "tbsp", "quantity": "1-2"}, {"item": "Garlic", "unit": "cloves", "notes": "minced", "quantity": "2"}, {"item": "Coconut aminos", "unit": "tbsp", "notes": "AIP-safe soy sauce substitute", "quantity": "2"}, {"item": "Sea salt", "unit": "", "quantity": "to taste"}, {"item": "Ground ginger", "unit": "tsp", "notes": "optional", "quantity": "1/2"}, {"item": "Fresh cilantro or green onion tops", "unit": "", "notes": "optional", "quantity": "for garnish"}],
    instructions: 'PREP\n====\n1. Cut broccoli into small, bite-sized florets.\n2. Halve zucchini lengthwise and slice into 1/4-inch half-moons.\n3. Mince garlic. Slice avocado (set aside for topping).\n\nCOOK THE BISON\n==============\n1. Heat 1 tbsp oil in a large skillet or wok over medium-high heat.\n2. Add ground bison and break apart with a spatula.\n3. Cook 5-7 minutes until browned and cooked through.\n4. Season with salt and optional ginger. Remove and set aside.\n\nSTIR FRY THE VEGGIES\n====================\n1. In the same skillet, add another splash of oil if needed.\n2. Add broccoli florets and cook 3-4 minutes, stirring frequently, until bright green and slightly charred but still crisp.\n3. Add zucchini and garlic. Cook another 2-3 minutes until zucchini is just tender.\n4. Season with salt.\n\nCOMBINE & FINISH\n================\n1. Return bison to the skillet with the veggies.\n2. Drizzle coconut aminos over everything and toss to coat.\n3. Cook 1 minute more to let flavors meld.\n4. Transfer to a plate and top with sliced avocado.\n5. Garnish with cilantro or green onion tops if desired.',
