    name: 'Coconut Curry Chicken',
    ingredients: [{"item": "Chicken thighs, boneless", "unit": "oz", "quantity": "10"}, {"item": "Full-fat coconut milk", "unit": "cup", "quantity": "1/2"}, {"item": "Cauliflower florets", "unit": "cup", "quantity": "1"}, {"item": "Carrots, sliced", "unit": "cup", "quantity": "1/2"}, {"item": "Fresh ginger, minced", "unit": "tbsp", "quantity": "1"}, {"item": "Turmeric powder", "unit": "tsp", "quantity": "1"}, {"item": "Garlic cloves, minced", "unit": "cloves", "quantity": "2"}, {"item": "Onion powder", "unit": "tsp", "quantity": "1/2"}, {"item": "Coconut oil", "unit": "tbsp", "quantity": "1"}, {"item": "Fresh cilantro, chopped", "unit": "tbsp", "quantity": "2"}, {"item": "Lime juice", "unit": "lime", "quantity": "1"}, {"item": "Sea salt", "unit": "tsp", "quantity": "1"}, {"item": "Fresh spinach", "unit": "cup", "quantity": "1"}],
    instructions: '1. Cut chicken thighs into bite-sized pieces. Season with turmeric, onion powder, and 1/2 tsp salt.\n\n2. Heat coconut oil in a large skillet or wok over medium-high heat.\n\n3. Add chicken and cook 4-5 minutes until browned. Remove and set aside.\n\n4. In the same pan, sauté ginger and garlic for 1 minute until fragrant.\n\n5. Add carrots and cauliflower. Cook 3-4 minutes.\n\n6. Pour in coconut milk and remaining salt. Stir and bring to a simmer.\n\n7. Return chicken to pan. Simmer 10-12 minutes until vegetables are tender and sauce thickens slightly.\n\n8. Stir in spinach until wilted. Remove from heat.\n\n9. Top with fresh cilantro and a squeeze of lime.\n\nNote: This is an AIP-safe "curry" using turmeric and ginger instead of traditional curry powder (which contains nightshades and seeds).\n\nFamily adaptation: Serve over jasmine rice for the family. They can add traditional curry paste or powder to their portions.\n\nMacros per serving:\n- Calories: ~750\n- Protein: 50g\n- Net Carbs: 12g\n- Fat: 45g',
