    ingredients: [{"item": "Ground beef (85% lean)", "unit": "oz", "quantity": "8"}, {"item": "Zucchini, diced", "unit": "medium", "quantity": "1"}, {"item": "Green beans", "unit": "cup", "quantity": "1"}, {"item": "Extra virgin olive oil", "unit": "tbsp", "quantity": "1"}, {"item": "Sea salt", "unit": "tsp", "quantity": "1/2"}, {"item": "Dried oregano", "unit": "tsp", "quantity": "1/2"}, {"item": "Fresh parsley, chopped", "unit": "tbsp", "quantity": "2"}],
    instructions: '1. Heat olive oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat.\n\n2. Add ground beef, breaking it up as it cooks.\n\n3. Season with salt and oregano.\n\n4. Cook until browned, about 6-8 minutes.\n\n5. Push beef to one side, add green beans to empty side.\n\n6. Cook green beans 4-5 minutes, stirring occasionally.\n\n7. Add zucchini and mix everything together.\n\n8. Cook another 3-4 minutes until zucchini is tender.\n\n9. Garnish with fresh parsley.\n\nGreat for meal prep - doubles well and reheats nicely.\n\nMacros per serving:\n- Calories: ~680\n- Protein: 48g\n- Net Carbs: 8g\n- Fat: 32g',
