    name: 'Honey Garlic Chicken with Roasted Root Vegetables',
    ingredients: [{"item": "Chicken breast", "unit": "oz", "quantity": "10"}, {"item": "Parsnips, cubed", "unit": "cup", "quantity": "1/2"}, {"item": "Carrots, cubed", "unit": "cup", "quantity": "1/2"}, {"item": "Turnips, cubed", "unit": "cup", "quantity": "1/2"}, {"item": "Raw honey", "unit": "tbsp", "quantity": "1"}, {"item": "Coconut aminos", "unit": "tbsp", "quantity": "2"}, {"item": "Garlic cloves, minced", "unit": "cloves", "quantity": "3"}, {"item": "Fresh ginger, minced", "unit": "tsp", "quantity": "1"}, {"item": "Avocado oil", "unit": "tbsp", "quantity": "2"}, {"item": "Sea salt", "unit": "tsp", "quantity": "1/2"}, {"item": "Fresh thyme", "unit": "sprigs", "quantity": "3-4"}, {"item": "Green onion, sliced", "unit": "tbsp", "quantity": "2"}],
    instructions: '1. Preheat oven to 400°F.\n\n2. Toss root vegetables (parsnips, carrots, turnips) with 1 tbsp avocado oil and salt. Spread on sheet pan with thyme sprigs.\n\n3. Roast vegetables for 15 minutes.\n\n4. Meanwhile, make the glaze: Whisk honey, coconut aminos, garlic, and ginger together.\n\n5. Slice chicken breast into thick strips or medallions. Season with salt.\n\n6. Heat remaining 1 tbsp avocado oil in an oven-safe skillet. Sear chicken 2 minutes per side.\n\n7. Pour honey garlic glaze over chicken. Transfer skillet to oven alongside vegetables.\n\n8. Roast 12-15 minutes until chicken reaches 165°F and glaze is sticky.\n\n9. Serve chicken over roasted vegetables. Garnish with green onions.\n\nFamily adaptation: This is delicious as-is for the whole family! They can add rice on the side. The honey garlic flavor is universally loved.\n\nMacros per serving:\n- Calories: ~680\n- Protein: 52g\n- Net Carbs: 22g\n- Fat: 28g',
    tags: ['aip', 'dinner', 'chicken', 'honey-garlic', 'sheet-pan', 'family-friendly', 'kid-friendly'],
