    ingredients: [{"item": "Chicken breast", "unit": "oz", "quantity": "10"}, {"item": "White sweet potato", "unit": "cup cubed", "quantity": "1/2"}, {"item": "Zucchini, sliced", "unit": "medium", "quantity": "1"}, {"item": "Fresh spinach", "unit": "cup", "quantity": "1"}, {"item": "Extra virgin olive oil", "unit": "tbsp", "quantity": "1"}, {"item": "Sea salt", "unit": "tsp", "quantity": "1/2"}, {"item": "Dried basil", "unit": "tsp", "quantity": "1/2"}],
    instructions: '1. Preheat oven to 400°F.\n\n2. Toss sweet potato cubes with half the olive oil and salt.\n\n3. Roast sweet potatoes for 15 minutes.\n\n4. Season chicken breast with salt and basil.\n\n5. Add chicken and zucchini to the pan with sweet potatoes.\n\n6. Drizzle remaining oil over chicken and zucchini.\n\n7. Roast another 20-25 minutes until chicken reaches 165°F.\n\n8. Serve over fresh spinach (the heat will wilt it slightly).\n\nMacros per serving:\n- Calories: ~720\n- Protein: 54g\n- Net Carbs: 19g\n- Fat: 24g',
